{"answers":[],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-9","impact":1,"impactReason":"This sets delivery scope, not product behavior, data, permissions, or visibility.","options":["Approve all 21 requirements for one implementation run.","Split into two runs: implement authentication, profiles, and administrator setup first; implement release, claim, verification, and reporting afterward.","Defer weekly utilization reporting (REQ-21–24) from this run and implement the remaining requirements."],"reason":"This preserves the full requested feature without changing its scope; run planning can be adjusted separately if needed.","recommended":"Approve all 21 requirements for one implementation run.","score":3,"spans":[],"text":"Should all 21 requirements be approved for one implementation run, or should the work be split or reduced?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-10","impact":2,"impactReason":"This changes the visible status flow, but not allocation rules or stored parking records.","options":["The release action confirms “Released”; the current parking status is “Claimable” once its availability time arrives (immediately for post-time same-day releases), then “Claimed” after allocation.","Use “Released” as the current status from release until a claim; represent claimability separately.","Use “Claimable” as the status as soon as the release is made, even when it cannot be claimed until the configured time."],"reason":"It preserves the release confirmation while making the current status accurately reflect when the space can be claimed.","recommended":"The release action confirms “Released”; the current parking status is “Claimable” once its availability time arrives (immediately for post-time same-day releases), then “Claimed” after allocation.","score":6,"spans":[],"text":"How should the release confirmation and the parking’s current status be represented when a release is not yet claimable, or becomes claimable immediately?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-11","impact":3,"impactReason":"Recipient controls determine who receives utilization reports.","options":["Drop the pre-authorization restriction; administrators can directly add, update, and remove report recipients.","Keep the restriction and seed the authorized stakeholder addresses during deployment; administrators can manage only those addresses afterward.","Keep the restriction and add an in-app approval workflow to authorize stakeholder addresses before administrators can select them."],"reason":"The request asks administrators to manage the stakeholder list but does not ask for a separate authorization mechanism.","recommended":"Drop the pre-authorization restriction; administrators can directly add, update, and remove report recipients.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Should administrators be able to add report recipients directly, or should the pre-authorization restriction remain, and if so, how should the initial authorized list be established?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"ASM-12 specifies email/password authentication with no SSO, directly contradicting REQ-1's mandatory Google Workspace sign-in.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-10 requires a release response to report `Released`, while REQ-12 requires a same-day release saved at or after the configured time to have status `Claimable`, leaving the same request with conflicting required statuses.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"ASM-27 permits administrators to select only pre-authorized stakeholder addresses, but no requirement defines how any address is initially authorized, so the recipient list cannot be populated through the specified system.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-14 requires push delivery to eligible employees but defines no device registration or notification-permission path, leaving the system without a specified way to identify reachable recipients or handle users who cannot receive push notifications.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-23 requires sending the report on Monday morning but specifies neither a clock time nor a configurable send time, so the scheduled trigger cannot be implemented or verified consistently.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"}],"lint":[{"blocking":true,"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 21 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","fails":["This spec has 21 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."],"passed":false},{"blocking":true,"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","fails":[],"hint":"Each Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes.","passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]}},"problemOf":{"Q-10":[3],"Q-11":[4],"Q-9":[1]},"problems":[{"kind":"lint","text":"L9 size: This spec has 21 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-1","text":"ASM-12 specifies email/password authentication with no SSO, directly contradicting REQ-1's mandatory Google Workspace sign-in."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-10","text":"REQ-10 requires a release response to report `Released`, while REQ-12 requires a same-day release saved at or after the configured time to have status `Claimable`, leaving the same request with conflicting required statuses."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-24","text":"ASM-27 permits administrators to select only pre-authorized stakeholder addresses, but no requirement defines how any address is initially authorized, so the recipient list cannot be populated through the specified system."}],"round":1,"settled":[],"spec":{"assumptions":["ASM-1: If Google authentication succeeds but the employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved from the corporate directory, deny access and return a retryable error with a contact path.","ASM-2 and ASM-13: A returning employee without a saved plate resumes vehicle registration and cannot proceed to the dashboard until at least one plate is saved.","ASM-3: The corporate directory is authoritative for employee identity; parking administrators maintain assignments, floors, and vehicles in the app.","ASM-4: Unreadable or unverifiable plates do not authorize entry, do not activate the green indicator, and are recorded with the failure reason.","ASM-5, ASM-17, and ASM-18: Camera, authorization, or indicator unavailability fails closed; no temporary entry authorization is issued and the outage or failed attempt is recorded.","ASM-6 and ASM-19: Administrators use admin-only screens in the same app; guard and administrator interfaces are responsive web interfaces for desktop and mobile browsers.","ASM-7: 'Today,' the 30-day scheduling window, and the Daily Parking Release Time use the office location's local timezone and calendar day.","ASM-8: For reporting, on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder.","ASM-9: For reporting, on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder.","ASM-10 and ASM-22: Initial user-facing content is English and left-to-right.","ASM-11 and ASM-23: The accessibility target is WCAG 2.1 AA on main flows.","ASM-12: If Google authentication succeeds but the corporate employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved, deny access and return a retryable error with a contact path.","ASM-14: Administrator plate changes affect future dates; existing claims retain the plate recorded when the claim was created.","ASM-15: An employee without dedicated parking may have at most one temporary claim per date.","ASM-17: If the camera, authorization service, or indicator is unavailable, fail closed and record or report the outage.","ASM-18: An unreadable or unmatched plate is unauthorized, keeps the green indicator off, and is recorded as a failed attempt.","ASM-19: Parking administrators and security guards use a responsive web app for desktop and mobile browsers; no native apps unless requirements name them.","ASM-20: For the weekly report, on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder.","ASM-21: For the report's overall utilization percentage, on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder.","ASM-22: Initial user-facing content is English and left-to-right.","ASM-23: The accessibility target is WCAG 2.1 AA on main flows.","ASM-24: The weekly report period is the preceding complete Monday-to-Sunday week in the office-local timezone.","ASM-25: Overall utilization percentage is unique parking-space days with a recorded actual entry divided by total active parking-space days in the report period, multiplied by 100.","ASM-26: The first parking administrator is provisioned from a deployment-controlled bootstrap setting containing an authorized Folio3 account; administrators maintain application role assignments thereafter.","ASM-27: Only email addresses pre-authorized as report stakeholders may receive weekly utilization reports; parking administrators may select and maintain the recipient list but cannot authorize additional addresses through that list."],"nfrs":[],"outOfScope":["Custom report builder (ASM-8, ASM-9)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has an authorized Folio3 Google Workspace account and an assigned application role","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the returned record contains the assigned role","when":"the user completes Google sign-in"},{"given":"A user signs in with a personal Gmail account or another non-Folio3 account","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 401 and no application session record is returned","when":"the authentication callback is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall accept sign-in only through authorized Folio3 Google Workspace accounts for employees, security guards, and parking administrators, rejecting personal Gmail and other provider accounts.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has a corporate-directory record and parking data entered in the app","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"the returned record contains the directory employee ID and name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle list","when":"the employee profile is retrieved"},{"given":"A parking administrator changes an employee's registered plate after a temporary claim has been created","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"the claim record contains the plate captured for that claim and the employee profile row contains the updated plate for future dates","when":"the claim record is retrieved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall identify employees by corporate email, retrieve employee ID and name from the corporate directory, and associate those identity fields with app-maintained dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and one or more registered vehicle profiles.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated non-dedicated employee has no saved plate","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 409 and the returned registration state requires at least one plate","when":"the employee requests the dashboard"},{"given":"An employee submits a vehicle profile with a plate and omits make, model, and color","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the vehicle row contains the plate with empty optional fields","when":"the profile is saved"}],"ears":"If a non-dedicated employee has no registered vehicle plate, then the Folio3 Parking System shall require at least one plate to be saved before making the dashboard available, while allowing vehicle make, model, and color to be optional and directing an incomplete returning profile to registration.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Google authentication succeeded but the employee profile is missing or unavailable","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 403, the error value is retryable, a contact path is returned, and no application session record exists","when":"the system completes profile lookup"}],"ears":"If Google authentication succeeds but the employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved from the corporate directory, then the Folio3 Parking System shall deny application access and return a retryable error with a contact path.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee, security guard, or parking administrator is authenticated","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"the response list contains only the employee's own records for an employee, verification information for a guard, and permitted managed records for an administrator","when":"each role requests employee and parking records"},{"given":"A security guard requests an administration function or an employee requests another employee's record","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 403 and no restricted record is returned","when":"the request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall restrict employees to their own records, limit guards to information needed for entry verification, and permit administrators to manage records and access configured reports.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-5","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator submits an initial parking-space inventory, associates a space with an assigned floor and dedicated holder, and enters the holder's vehicle","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the parking-space row contains its floor, the parking-assignment row references that space and holder, and the vehicle row contains the submitted values","when":"the administrator saves the records"},{"given":"A non-administrator submits an assignment, parking-space inventory, or vehicle maintenance request","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 403 and no record is changed","when":"the request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow parking administrators to enter and maintain the parking-space inventory, associate each space with an assigned floor and dedicated holder, and maintain employee parking assignments and registered vehicles, including initial launch records, with plate changes applying to future dates while existing claims retain their recorded plate.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","Q-1","Q-5","ASM-3","ASM-6","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder has not released today's parking","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the returned parking status is Released","when":"the holder submits the release action"},{"given":"A dedicated holder opens the employee home screen","id":"AC-10.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows a single release action and displays the resulting parking status","when":"the holder releases today's parking"},{"given":"A non-holder or a holder who has already released today's parking submits a release request","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"the response indicates an error and the parking row count for that holder and date remains one","when":"the request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall let only a dedicated parking holder release today's parking through a single home-screen release action, prevent duplicate releases for the same holder and date, and expose the current Reserved, Released, or Claimed status.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder selects a date 30 local calendar days ahead","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and a release row exists for the selected date","when":"the holder saves the scheduled release"},{"given":"A dedicated holder selects a date 31 local calendar days ahead","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 422 and no release row exists for that date","when":"the holder submits the scheduled release"},{"given":"A dedicated holder opens the release calendar","id":"AC-11.3","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows the selected dates as scheduled releases","when":"the holder selects and saves multiple dates within the 30-day window"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall let dedicated holders schedule releases for one or multiple future dates up to 30 calendar days ahead and persist each selected release.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No administrator has changed the Daily Parking Release Time","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"the returned value is 08:00 in the office-local timezone","when":"the configuration is retrieved"},{"given":"A release is scheduled for today or is submitted before the configured time","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"the release row status is Claimable","when":"the configured Daily Parking Release Time is reached"},{"given":"A holder submits a same-day release at or after the configured time","id":"AC-12.3","level":"api","then":"the release row status is Claimable and the available-space count is updated","when":"the release is saved"},{"given":"An administrator submits a new Daily Parking Release Time","id":"AC-12.4","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the returned configuration contains the new time","when":"the configuration is saved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall use a configurable Daily Parking Release Time defaulting to 08:00 office-local time, make pre-scheduled releases and same-day releases created before that time claimable at that time, and make same-day releases created at or after that time claimable immediately.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One or more spaces become claimable and eligible employees without dedicated parking exist","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains the refreshed available-space count and an outbound call to the push notification service is sent to eligible employees","when":"availability is updated"},{"given":"An employee opens the availability view","id":"AC-14.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the current available-space count","when":"the view is loaded"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall publish the current available-space count and send a push notification to eligible employees without dedicated parking whenever one or more spaces become claimable.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Two eligible employees concurrently request the last available space","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"the first accepted request has a successful response, the later response contains an error, and the later response includes the refreshed available-space count","when":"the service accepts the requests in a defined order"},{"given":"An employee already has a temporary claim for a date or has dedicated parking","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"the response contains an error and the claim row count for that employee and date remains one","when":"the employee requests another temporary claim for that date"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee request accepted by the service, limit each employee to one temporary claim per date, and return refreshed availability to later unsuccessful claimants.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-3","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An eligible employee successfully claims an available space","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains the assigned floor and a claim row contains the date, time, employee, and assigned-space fields","when":"the claim is completed"},{"given":"A claim is returned to an employee","id":"AC-16.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the assigned floor without requiring floor-arrival confirmation","when":"the employee views the claim"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall assign one available parking space and its floor to a successful claimant, record the claim date, time, employee, and assigned space for audit, and not require proof that the employee parked on the assigned floor.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has an active temporary claim","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200, the claim row status is Cancelled, and the available-space count increases immediately","when":"the employee cancels the claim"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow an employee to cancel a successful temporary claim at any time and make the claimed space available immediately.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The LPR camera sends car, pedestrian, motorcycle, and other non-car detections","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"the returned event list contains car detections and contains no verification request for the non-car detections","when":"the detection events are processed"},{"given":"A vehicle is marked as having a permanent parking sticker","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"the verification request count is zero and no temporary authorization call is made","when":"its entrance event is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall process license-plate-recognition detections for cars, ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects, and bypass temporary system verification for vehicles marked with a permanent parking sticker.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A temporary claim is active for today and the detected plate is any plate registered to its claimant for the claimed date","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"the authorization response is valid and an outbound call to the indicator controller requests green","when":"the plate is verified"},{"given":"A detected plate has no valid temporary claim for today","id":"AC-19.2","level":"api","then":"the authorization response is invalid and the green-indicator activation call count is zero","when":"the plate is verified"}],"ears":"Where a readable plate is detected on an unstickered vehicle, the Folio3 Parking System shall verify it against a temporary claim for the current office-local date using any plate registered to the claimant for the claimed date and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-2","ASM-7","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The LPR service returns an unreadable plate, an unmatched plate, or an unavailable-service error","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"the error or event record contains the failure reason and the green-indicator activation call count is zero","when":"the entrance verification is processed"},{"given":"The indicator controller is unavailable","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"the response contains an error, an outage event row is recorded, and no automated authorization is returned","when":"a verification is attempted"}],"ears":"If a plate is unreadable or unverifiable, or the camera, authorization service, or indicator is unavailable, then the Folio3 Parking System shall make no automated authorization, issue no green-indicator activation, and record an unreadable, unverifiable, or outage event.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-4","ASM-5","ASM-17","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A temporary verification attempt has completed and the guard records whether the vehicle entered","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"the verification record row contains the date, time, plate or unreadable status, verification result, and actual-entry status","when":"the entry outcome is saved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall record every temporary verification attempt with its date, time, detected plate or unreadable status, and verification result, and let security record whether the vehicle actually entered after the check.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated space was not released and has no actual-entry record, or a temporary claim has no actual-entry record","id":"AC-22.1","level":"job","then":"a utilization event row identifies the employee, vehicle, date, and Unused Dedicated Parking or Unused Temporary Parking classification as applicable","when":"the utilization job processes the date"},{"given":"A camera detection or authorization exists without a guard-recorded actual entry","id":"AC-22.2","level":"job","then":"the utilization event row does not classify the parking as utilized solely from that detection or authorization","when":"the utilization job processes the date"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall use recorded actual-entry outcomes, rather than camera detections or authorization attempts alone, to preserve utilization history and identify dedicated parking that was not released and had no entry and temporary claims that had no entry.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The weekly reporting job is due on Monday morning and recipient addresses are configured","id":"AC-23.1","level":"job","then":"the report record covers the preceding complete Monday-to-Sunday office-local week and contains the required employee lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space count, temporary-claim count, and numeric utilization percentage","when":"the reporting job runs"},{"given":"The weekly reporting job runs on Monday morning","id":"AC-23.2","level":"job","then":"an outbound call to the email delivery service contains the report and is addressed to every configured stakeholder","when":"the report is generated"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall generate and email a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office-local timezone to configured stakeholders, containing unused dedicated and temporary parking employees, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and temporary-claim totals, and an overall utilization percentage.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-7","ASM-24","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated administrator submits email addresses already authorized as report stakeholders","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the recipient-list row contains the submitted addresses","when":"the recipient list is saved"},{"given":"An administrator opens report settings in the app","id":"AC-24.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the saved recipient list","when":"the administrator updates the stakeholder list"},{"given":"An authenticated administrator submits an address that is not authorized as a report stakeholder","id":"AC-24.3","level":"api","then":"the response contains an error and the recipient-list row does not contain the unauthorized address","when":"the recipient list is saved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall allow parking administrators to add, update, and remove the stakeholder list used for weekly utilization report emails in the app, accepting only addresses already authorized as report stakeholders.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-8","ASM-6","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A deployment configuration contains the authorized Folio3 account designated as the initial administrator","id":"AC-26.1","level":"job","then":"an application role record exists for that account with the parking-administrator role","when":"the application bootstrap job runs"},{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator assigns an application role to an authorized Folio3 account","id":"AC-26.2","level":"api","then":"the response status is 200 and the role-assignment row contains the account and assigned role","when":"the role assignment is saved"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking System shall provision the first parking administrator from a deployment-configured Folio3 account and let administrators assign employee, security-guard, and administrator roles to other authorized Folio3 accounts.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1","Q-7","ASM-26"]}]}}